---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { alternatesFor, staticPath, homePath } from '../../i18n/config.js';
import { t } from '../../i18n/ui.js';

const locale = 'en';
const strings = t(locale);
const pageId = 'privacy';
const path = staticPath(pageId, locale);
const alternates = alternatesFor('static', pageId);
const lastUpdated = 'July 7, 2026';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | Check and Validate';
const description =
  'How Check and Validate handles cookies, Google AdSense advertising, and your data, explained in plain language.';

const schema = {
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: strings.breadcrumbHome, item: new URL(homePath(locale), Astro.site).toString() },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Privacy Policy', item: new URL(path, Astro.site).toString() },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} locale={locale} path={path} alternates={alternates} schema={schema}>
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href={homePath(locale)}>{strings.breadcrumbHome}</a>
    <span class="sep">&gt;</span>
    <span aria-current="page">Privacy Policy</span>
  </nav>

  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="disclaimer">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

  <p>
    This page explains what data Check and Validate collects, why, and how you can control it. We
    have kept it in plain language rather than dense legal text.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
  <p>
    Every validator on this site runs entirely in your browser. The numbers you type into a tool,
    such as a CNP, a DNI, a NIE, or an IBAN, are never sent to a server, stored in a database, or
    seen by anyone else. There is no account system and nothing to sign up for.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This site uses cookies for two purposes: to remember whether you have accepted or declined the
    cookie notice, and to support the advertising described below. Your browser lets you block or
    delete cookies at any time through its settings, though doing so may cause the cookie banner to
    reappear on your next visit.
  </p>

  <h2>Google AdSense and third-party advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Check and Validate uses Google AdSense to show ads, which is how the site stays free. Google
    and other third-party advertising vendors use cookies to serve ads based on a visitor's prior
    visits to this site and to other sites across the web. This is sometimes called interest-based
    or personalized advertising. It works by tracking browsing patterns at the browser or device
    level, not by identifying who you are, and it does not include personal identifiers such as
    your name, home address, or email address.
  </p>
  <p>
    Google's own explanation of how it and its partners handle data collected on sites that use its
    services is available at
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your advertising choices</h2>
  <p>
    If you would prefer not to see personalized ads, you can adjust your settings directly with
    Google at
    <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">adssettings.google.com</a>,
    or use the industry-wide opt-out tools at
    <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a>.
    Both let you opt out of interest-based advertising across many participating sites and
    advertisers, not just this one.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can also disable cookies entirely through your browser's settings, which applies to the
    cookies used for advertising as well as the one this site uses to remember your cookie banner
    choice. Doing so may cause some conveniences, such as remembering that choice between visits, to
    stop working as expected.
  </p>

  <h2>Visitors in the European Economic Area and the United Kingdom</h2>
  <p>
    Because this site serves visitors in the European Union, including Romania and Spain, and in
    the United Kingdom, visitors in those regions are shown a consent message that lets them choose
    whether to allow personalized advertising, in line with Google's certified consent
    requirements. Your choice is remembered so you are not asked on every visit.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This site may use a privacy-conscious analytics tool to understand overall traffic, such as
    which pages are visited and roughly how many people visit, so the site can be improved. Any
    analytics used here does not identify you personally and is separate from the advertising
    cookies described above.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    This site is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect personal
    information from them.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this page with a new "last
    updated" date at the top.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy can be sent to
    <a href="mailto:contact@checkandvalidate.com">contact@checkandvalidate.com</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
